{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nexp=d.pop('experiment')\nexp['previous_id']='981f67969ef44bc1b4d8e296cbb610c4-experiment'\nexp['revision_reason']=(\\\"The executed run confirmed the membership resurrection but never reached the write prediction: the retained log shows B winning the election in term 3 right after A's restart, so A was a follower when the write was issued and the Apply returned a leadership error. Two harness faults are corrected: B's heartbeat/election timeouts are reloaded to 3s before A restarts so the stale leader wins its re-election, and the harness now records whether A is leader before the partition and takes the compared index from the Apply future itself, emitting the quorum field only when the write was acknowledged. C's own restart is also kept on the normal path (flag disabled) so a configuration-less C cannot confound the election.\\\")\n# comparisons: gate the write comparison on A actually leading\nexp['prerequisites']=[\n {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_on\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"before_restart_restore_on\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_on\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":2}]},\n {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_off\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"before_restart_restore_off\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_off\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":2}]},\n {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_write_on\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"split_setup_restore_on\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_on\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_is_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}]},\n {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_write_off\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"split_setup_restore_off\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_off\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_is_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}]},\n]\nexp['comparisons'][2]={\\\"event\\\":\\\"split_write_restore_on\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_write_on\\\",\n \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"entry_on_quorum\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"An entry whose Apply reported success on the stale-membership leader must be present on a quorum of the configuration committed in the log ({A,B} requires both members).\\\"}\nexp['comparisons'][3]={\\\"event\\\":\\\"split_write_restore_off\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_write_off\\\",\n \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"write_applied\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: with the committed membership the same partition must make the leader refuse the write.\\\"}\nd['experiment']=exp\n# new child interpretation\nchild={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"981f67969ef44bc1b4d8e296cbb610c4-question-1\\\",\n \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"981f67969ef44bc1b4d8e296cbb610c4-experiment\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"newraft_scan\\\",\\\"restore_committed\\\",\\\"snapshot_config\\\",\\\"commit_config_on_append\\\",\\\"vote_prevote_checks\\\"],\n \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"ee57ec0448704270bcbc1cf7ace9a045\\\":[1]},\n \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"explained\\\",\n \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"unresolved\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Retained receipt ee57ec0448704270bcbc1cf7ace9a045 establishes the membership half of this question: after a committed RemoveServer of the offline voter C and a restart with RestoreCommittedLogs, the restarted leader reports three servers including C and two peers while the continuously running member B reports two servers and one peer (comparison 0 violated, witness index 1). The write half was not reached in that execution: B won the election in term 3 immediately after A's restart (as the run log shows) and A was a follower when the write was issued, so the Apply returned a leadership error, the entry index in the observation was the pre-existing no-op and the quorum field was therefore vacuous; that comparison is recorded as not reached and is not used as evidence. The corrected harness (successor requested in this update) keeps the stale leader in power, records whether A leads before the partition and takes the compared index from the Apply future, so the premature-commit question can be decided by a retained receipt.\\\"),\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"In the same receipt the control mode kept the committed membership (two servers) and the write prediction was not reached there either, so nothing in this receipt supports the premature-commit claim in either direction.\\\"],\n \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"The premature-commit claim rests on a construction-time run of the corrected harness only; its retained receipt is requested in this update and until it exists the child defect judgment stays unresolved.\\\",\n  \\\"That construction-time run needed an explicit re-election setup (B's timeouts reloaded) because the stale leader otherwise loses the first election to a member with the correct configuration; the accounting is a property of the configurations, not of those timeouts.\\\"]\n}\nd['interpretations'].append(child)\npar=d['interpretations'][0]\npar['limitations']=[l for l in par['limitations'] if 'resurrected-voter decision consequence' not in l]\npar['limitations'] += [\n \\\"The child question's retained receipt (ee57ec0448704270bcbc1cf7ace9a045) confirmed the resurrected membership but did not reach the premature-commit observation, because the stale leader lost the post-restart election to the correctly configured member in that execution; the child interpretation records this and requests the corrected harness.\\\"]\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
